## 3. Reduction method

**Algorithm: DRGEP** (directed relation graph with error propagation;
Lu & Law 2005; Pepiot-Desjardins & Pitsch 2008), implemented from scratch
(`scripts/drgep.py`) for full inspectability:

* State sampling: adiabatic constant-volume autoignition trajectories over
  192 conditions per tier (8 fuels × φ{0.5,1,2} × T0{1050,1300,1600,1900 K} ×
  P{1,10 atm}), ~20 states per trajectory spread over the temperature rise
  (2932 states total).
* Direct coefficients r_AB = |Σ ν_A,i ω_i δ_B,i| / max(P_A, C_A),
  path coefficients by Dijkstra max-product search from target species
  (fuels + O2/N2/AR/H2O/CO2), overall importance R_B = max over targets
  and sampled states.
* **Modification:** an activity floor — species rows with max(P_A,C_A) below
  1e-15 × state maximum are zeroed. Without it, frozen channels
  (rates ~1e-137) produce spurious r ≈ 1 edges that glue dead branches
  (e.g. benzene) into the graph even for the H2/CO/CH4 tier. With the floor,
  the GRI-Mech 3.0 benchmark is unchanged (39/53 species at ε = 0.3,
  chemically sensible removals: NOx and C3 minors first).
* Threshold sweep ε ∈ {0.4 … 0.015} per tier → candidate mechanisms built by
  textual YAML subsetting (`scripts/mech_tools.py`): rate data, thermo and
  transport are preserved verbatim; third-body efficiencies of removed
  colliders are dropped; reactions involving removed species are dropped.

**Tool check:** the DRGEP implementation was benchmarked against
Cantera-bundled GRI-Mech 3.0 (53 species): reductions of 39–50 species over
ε = 0.3–0.01 with chemically sensible ordering, consistent with published
DRG/DRGEP behaviour on that mechanism.

**Consistency checks:** all reduced mechanisms load in Cantera (elemental
balance enforced), and adiabatic flame temperatures match the parent exactly
(e.g. CH4/air φ = 1: 2230.3 K before and after reduction) since thermo is
inherited unchanged.

