## 9. How retrieved knowledge changed the plan

* The **FFCM-2 validation pages** (found by following the SFCPD pointer from
  the task brief) provided a complete, citable experimental target set with
  uncertainties and references; this replaced the planned hand-assembly of
  literature data and fixed the experimental case list.
* The **target fuel coverage of the FFCM-2 set** (C0–C4, no pure CO,
  HE diluents present) directly shaped the tier fuel list and the HE
  exclusion.
* **USC-II literature practice** (its own validation domain: high-T, C1–C4)
  motivated the explicit domain narrowing away from C4+/aromatics, with the
  consequences stated in §1.
* **DRG/DRGEP methodology papers** (Lu & Law 2005; Pepiot & Pitsch 2008)
  fixed the reduction algorithm; the GRI-Mech 3.0 benchmark confirmed the
  implementation; the frozen-channel failure observed here motivated the
  activity-floor modification.
* Unavailable resources (SFCPD direct download, ReSpecTh API, ChemKED via
  blocked github.com) were reported rather than assumed.

## 10. Stopping rationale

The delivered Pareto set is stable: fidelity knee located (62/49 sp for
C0–C1; 86 sp for C0–C3), experimental equivalence to the parent demonstrated
at all three levels, and consistency checks pass. Further compression (e.g.
2nd-stage reaction pruning, ~20 % fewer reactions) was scoped but deferred
as marginal; further domain widening (C4+) contradicts the compression
objective. Remaining budget is therefore spent on documentation rather than
on candidates with diminishing scientific return.

